From: System Electronics
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: waveshare-dsi: log which panel the device tree selected

The MCU exposes nothing readable: there is no ID or version register, and
no public register map exists for it. The driver therefore cannot detect
which panel is physically attached, and put in front of the wrong one it
"succeeds" and drives it at the wrong resolution, producing a broken
image with no error anywhere in the log.

With more than one device tree shipping this driver, that is the trap
waiting for whoever selects the wrong one. Failing cleanly is not
possible, so state at probe what the device tree asked for.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-waveshare-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-waveshare-dsi.c
@@ -464,6 +464,7 @@
 		.node = NULL,
 	};
 	const struct ws_panel_data *_ws_panel_data;
+	const char *compat = NULL;
 	int ret;
 
 	ts = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*ts), GFP_KERNEL);
@@ -482,6 +483,19 @@
 
 	ts->i2c = i2c;
 
+	/*
+	 * The MCU exposes nothing readable: there is no ID register, so the
+	 * driver cannot tell which panel is actually attached and will happily
+	 * drive a different one at the wrong resolution, with no error in the
+	 * log. With more than one device tree shipping this driver, say what
+	 * the device tree asked for, so a wrong choice is visible at boot.
+	 */
+	of_property_read_string(dev->of_node, "compatible", &compat);
+	dev_info(dev, "Waveshare panel '%s' at %pOF: %ux%u@%u, %d lane(s)\n",
+		 compat ? compat : "unknown", dev->of_node,
+		 ts->mode->hdisplay, ts->mode->vdisplay,
+		 drm_mode_vrefresh(ts->mode), _ws_panel_data->lanes);
+
 	ret = of_drm_get_panel_orientation(dev->of_node, &ts->orientation);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "%pOF: failed to get orientation %d\n", dev->of_node, ret);
